(* newspeak-spec.pdf 3.6: an activation has "zero or more parameter slots,
   one for each formal parameter of p. Parameter slots are immutable
   (6.3.2)", and 6.3.2 gives an immutable slot a getter alone -- "There is
   no setter method associated with the slot". So no construct lexically
   enclosing the write declares `value:`, and 5.7 makes the setter send
   `value:: 9` -- "equivalent to the expression `[:p | id:p. p] value:(e)`"
   (5.4.3) -- the self send `value: 9`, which nothing answers. The same
   rule spec_6_3_2_immutable_slot_has_no_setter pins for a declared
   immutable slot, and this records its stderr.

   The resolver binds a parameter to a writable register like any local, so
   the write lands and the method answers 9 at exit status 0. Skipped until
   a parameter refuses its setter. *)
class Spec36ParameterIsImmutable = Object new () (
    replace: value = ( value:: 9. ^value )
    public main: platform args: arguments = (
        | t = platform transcript. |
        t show: (self replace: 1) printString; newLine.
    )
) : ()
